# Animation Event Callback Checklist

When adding or renaming any public animation-event callback method (for example on `Combat`, `SimpleEnemyAI`, forwarders, or related animation receiver components):

- Add/update the method in `Assets/Features/Combat/Editor/AnimationEventMethodCatalog.cs` curated entries so it appears in `Tools > Combat > Animation Event Authoring` curated mode.
- Add/update the method reference in `Assets/Features/Combat/AnimationEventFunctions.md` with short behavior notes.
- If the callback uses an `int` parameter, add/update descriptor metadata in the JSON block in `Assets/Features/Combat/AnimationEventFunctions.md` so the authoring window shows clear labels/help/presets.
- Keep method names and signatures consistent between runtime scripts, curated catalog labels, and docs.

Do not rely only on reflection mode for newly added production callbacks; keep curated entries updated.
